    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is centered around **Daulton Varsho**, who leads the board with a 72.31 efficiency score. His matchup against the high-xERA arm of Quantrill provides a massive 19% SP skill boost, and with his consistent stolen base upside against a slow delivery, he is our premier option. **Taylor Ward** (67.91) also presents a high-floor play; he benefits significantly from a +16% park factor and a top-of-the-order slot, making him a cornerstone of today's scoring strategy. We are also capitalizing on favorable matchup conditions for **Tyler Freeman** (65.23) and **Jonathan Aranda** (64.32), both of whom are projected to thrive against middling starting pitchers, with **Jonathan Aranda** specifically benefiting from an elite xwOBA trend and a positive platoon split.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Jeremiah Jackson**, whose 46.37 score fell just shy of the cutoff. While he benefits from the same park environment as **Taylor Ward**, the combined drag of a lower-tier batting order position and the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time suppressed his steal probability, pushing him behind the more efficient options currently in our starting nine. Similarly, **Gavin Sheets** could not overcome a difficult matchup against Yamamoto, leaving him on the bench to preserve our game caps. Investors should remain mindful of the 100% stolen base opportunity window against the pitchers facing **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Daulton Varsho**; their efficiency scores are buoyed by the expectation of aggressive base running against slow-to-the-plate arms. Note that **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** remain unavailable due to IL status, requiring us to rely on our active depth to keep pace in the SB category.",
